  "solution": "Logic : 1st number = (2nd number × 3rd number)\n\nGiven : \n\n \n• (312, 24, 13)\n\n312 = 24 × 13 \n\n312 = 312 (LHS = RHS)\n\n \n• (645, 43, 15)\n\n645 = 43 × 15\n\n645 = 645 (LHS = RHS)\n\nSo,\n\n \n• Option - (1) : (347, 27, 12) \n\n347 = 27 × 12\n\n347 ≠ 324 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\n \n• Option - (2) : (347, 22, 17) \n\n347 = 22 × 17\n\n347 ≠ 374 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\n \n• Option - (3) : (374, 17, 12) \n\n374 = 17 × 12\n\n374 ≠ 204 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\n \n• Option - (4) : (374, 22, 17) \n\n374 = 22 × 17\n\n374 = 374 (LHS = RHS) \n\nHence, \"Option - (4)\" is the correct answer.",
